    "forge": "github",
    "question": "1: raw accept on a directory, a symlink, a submodule and an LFS pointer",
    "source": "torvalds/linux, git/git, Unity-Technologies/BoatAttack (public)",
    "finding": "Only a regular file or a symlink answers with Content-Type application/vnd.github.raw. A directory answers 200 with an application/json array and a submodule 200 with an application/json object of type 'submodule', so a reader must check the Content-Type and refuse anything that is not the raw media type. A symlink answers its target path as the body. An LFS-tracked file answers the pointer text, not the object, with no redirect."
